# Local apartment-hunt pipeline data (derived, large, or listing-sourced)
research/pipeline/*.sqlite
research/pipeline/*.sqlite-shm
research/pipeline/*.sqlite-wal
research/pipeline/*.json
# ...except the inputs a clone needs to build the page without scraping. The
# sanitised set carries no owner names, no phone numbers and no landlord field
# beyond a registration flag; it is the same corpus already published at the
# hosted demo, so committing it exposes nothing new and makes the repo
# runnable instead of merely readable.
!research/pipeline/app_data.public.json
!research/pipeline/street_grid.json
!research/pipeline/places.json
research/pipeline/huntly_built.html
# The OSM extract (72MB) is rebuildable and huge. The routing graph derived
# from it is committed: 1.5MB, and without it every distance silently degrades
# to a straight line, which is the one claim this project exists to stop making.
research/pipeline/sf.osm.gz
research/pipeline/walk_tiles/
# Built demo pages inline the entire scraped data set -- ~6.7MB each, including
# the owner-entity names add_landlord.py reads out of public records. Those are
# live-path only, by the same rule that keeps them out of fixtures/demo.sqlite,
# so no built page belongs in the public tree. The sources that build them do.
research/*-demo.html
# The Vercel deploy directory. Its index.html is the sanitised build, so it
# carries no owner names or phone numbers -- but it is still a 7.5MB generated
# artefact rebuilt by `sanitize_public.py && build_pages.py --public`, and
# .vercel/ and .env.local inside it hold project ids and an OIDC token.
research/public/
# Scratch from individual pipeline runs: slug dumps the scrapers page through,
# Apify run ids, and sweep logs. All of it is regenerated by the next run and
# none of it means anything to a reader -- `apify_run.txt` is a bare run id,
# which is exactly the "one-off operational detail" the public-repo contract
# says to keep out.
research/pipeline/*.txt
research/pipeline/*.log
# Scraped listing dump left at the repo root by a one-off Apify test. Half a
# megabyte of third-party listing data, and a byte-identical copy already sits
# under research/pipeline/ where the rest of the scraped JSON is ignored.
apify_test.json
